[^876]: The word [{_falcare_}]{lang=lat}, in French [{_faucher_}]{lang=fra}, here translated “curve,” is a term of equitation, describing the motion of the outer foreleg of a horse in going round in a circle. It is the sweep of a mower’s scythe.

